From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: wm_reader profile and stream configuration (IWMProfile, IWMStreamConfig, IWMMediaProps, output props names, INSSBuffer::GetLength, mutual exclusion / bandwidth sharing / stream prioritization objects)

Stubs of the sync reader's WMV objects, as the Windows Media Format SDK
documents them:

- String properties follow the SDK buffer protocol: a NULL buffer returns
  the length needed (characters, NUL included), a short buffer returns it
  with ASF_E_BUFFERTOOSMALL, a NULL length is E_INVALIDARG. Used by
  IWMStreamConfig::Get/SetStreamName and Get/SetConnectionName,
  IWMProfile::Get/SetName and Get/SetDescription,
  IWMOutputMediaProps::GetStreamGroupName / GetConnectionName (an output of
  a file reader has no group or connection: empty strings).
- INSSBuffer::GetLength returns the current length.
- IWMStreamConfig: stream number 1..63 (E_INVALIDARG otherwise), bitrate,
  buffer window (-1 when unset), media type through IWMMediaProps
  (GetType, SetMediaType, E_INVALIDARG for NULL or another major type).
  A config is a copy: edits reach the profile with ReconfigStream.
- IWMProfile of a reader: GetVersion, GetProfileID (GUID_NULL), storage
  format (V1 default, MP3), RemoveStream / RemoveStreamByNumber
  (NS_E_NO_STREAM when absent), AddStream (NS_E_INVALID_STREAM when the
  number is taken), ReconfigStream, CreateNewStream (lowest free number),
  GetExpectedPacketCount (bitrates over the duration in 3200-byte packets).
  Only the profile view changes; the streams the reader delivers do not.
- IWMMutualExclusion, IWMBandwidthSharing and IWMStreamPrioritization
  objects with their profile Get/Add/Remove/CreateNew calls.
  Removing a stream from the profile removes it from those lists.

